---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Layout title="About — LluckyGames" wide>
  <div class="text-column">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>
    I'm <strong>Lluc Sansaloni</strong> — a systems person with a games heart,
    based in Munich. By day I've spent five years keeping production systems
    alive (Linux, Windows, Azure, automation); by training I'm a video game
    designer (Grado Superior in 3D Animation &amp; Video Games, LADAT).
    LluckyGames is where those two halves meet.
  </p>

  <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
  <p>
    Most portfolios show <em>what</em> someone made. This one also shows
    <em>how they think</em> about the systems players actually live inside —
    the economies of live-service games, where a misaligned currency bundle is
    a design decision with a number attached.
  </p>
  <p>Two tracks:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Writing</strong> — taking live-service economies apart with real
      data (Riot's RP pricing, the WoW Token, Warframe's platinum market), and
      ending every essay with what I'd design differently.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Prototypes</strong> — small playable builds that isolate one
      system each. First up: a rock-paper-scissors combat resolver with HP,
      mana and a readable AI.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What I bring</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Data over vibes</strong> — five years of production systems teach
      you to measure before you opine. The essays use real prices, real rates.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>I ship the prototype myself</strong> — TypeScript, web builds, no
      waiting for an engineer to make the design question testable.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Systems thinking</strong> — economies, networks, permission
      models: I already think in interdependent parts. Games are just friendlier
      graphs.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Now</h2>
  <p>
    Pivoting from IT operations toward <strong>game design</strong> — targeting
    systems/economy design roles in the European live-service scene. Open to
    junior and mid roles, Munich or remote-friendly.
  </p>

  <div class="btn-row">
    <a class="btn" href={`${base}/contact/`}>Get in touch</a>
    <a class="btn ghost" href={`${base}/writing/`}>Read the essays</a>
  </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
